  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kentucky has $8.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 83,354 awards with an average award size of $105K, and obligations fell 16.0% year over year. Totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $7.9B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations, receiving $5.6B. HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC is the largest vendor by obligations at $5.6B, followed by LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $618M and THALLE - BAUER LLC at $378M. Recent fiscal-year history shows obligations peaked at $12.5B in FY23 and then moved to $12.3B in FY24, $10.4B in FY25, and $8.8B in FY26 to date. Other notable buying agencies include the Department of the Treasury with $203M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $178M. Industries beyond insurance with material obligations include All Other Support Services at $623M and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $403M.",
